WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.280 line:84% position:0% align:start size:76%
By default, viaduct gives you a random name, and a new one every time you reconnect. That's

00:00:05.280 --> 00:00:09.200 line:84% position:0% align:start size:76%
fine for a quick look, but for a webhook or a link you're sharing you may want something a bit

00:00:09.200 --> 00:00:16.680 line:84% position:0% align:start size:76%
more meaningful. If you try to reach a domain that doesn't exist, or isn't registered,

00:00:16.680 --> 00:00:22.540 line:84% position:0% align:start size:76%
you see this default holding page. These holding pages are per region; by default

00:00:22.540 --> 00:00:27.720 line:84% position:0% align:start size:76%
I'm connecting to London, and this one is currently not in use for my demo app. So

00:00:27.720 --> 00:00:34.240 line:84% position:0% align:start size:76%
I'm going to reserve it. To do that I'll ask viaduct http to map to

00:00:34.240 --> 00:00:37.760 line:84% position:0% align:start size:76%
the local demo app running on my machine, and use the --name parameter. I'm

00:00:37.760 --> 00:00:44.760 line:84% position:0% align:start size:76%
going to pick a name, and if it's free it will reserve it for me. So now if I go to

00:00:44.760 --> 00:00:54.360 line:84% position:0% align:start size:76%
this address and refresh, this is now mine. Nobody else can reserve it. The moment the

00:00:54.360 --> 00:01:00.480 line:84% position:0% align:start size:76%
tunnel dies it becomes reservable for others. So it's a nice, quick way to create

00:01:00.480 --> 00:01:04.800 line:84% position:0% align:start size:76%
a custom, shareable name that's memorable. And that's custom names.
